{{!-- One result of a move: its notation in a band, and what the move says happens there.

      The move item sheet and the season box both draw a move's 10+/7-9/6-, and they had drawn them
      twice — a labelled table on the item sheet, a two-column list of accent-coloured notation in
      the season box — off the same authored `system.moveResults`. One partial, so the three results
      of a move are one thing wherever they are read.

      Params: key (success/partial/failure — the tint), label (the move's own notation), text (the
      result, a RichText or a string; omitted where the caller's own body renders it instead),
      rolled (this is the row the dice landed on), and the SLOT: `bodyPartial`, the name of a partial
      to render under the text, with `body` as its context.

      The slot is what keeps the two surfaces one component while they differ in what a row can DO:
      the item sheet's body is the textarea that authors the text, and the season's is everything the
      steading has built that waits on this result, plus the roll that result costs.

      It is a NAMED PARTIAL and not a `{{#> }}` block on purpose. Handlebars renders partial-block
      content with the prototype-access runtime options stripped, silently — every getter inside the
      block reads as undefined, so the season's rows lost their controls and their clauses with
      nothing thrown and no blank where they had been (verified against Handlebars 4.7.9). Passing
      the object through `body` and rendering it as an ordinary partial keeps it whole: a hash param
      is a reference, so the row a body partial receives is the snapshot itself, getters included.

      `rolled` is a reading of the dice, not a state of the move, so it is never said in colour
      alone: the band says it in words, because colour is not a thing every reader gets (WCAG 1.4.1),
      and `aria-current` is what says it to the ones who hear the page. --}}
<div class="stonetop-result-row stonetop-result-row--{{key}}{{#if rolled}} is-rolled{{/if}}"
     {{#if rolled}}aria-current="true"{{/if}}>
	<span class="stonetop-result-label">
		<span class="stonetop-result-notation">{{label}}</span>
		{{#if rolled}}<span class="stonetop-result-rolled">{{localize "stonetop.rollResults.rolled"}}</span>{{/if}}
	</span>
	<div class="stonetop-result-body">
		{{#if (hasText text)}}<div class="stonetop-result-text stonetop-rich">{{rich text}}</div>{{/if}}
		{{#if bodyPartial}}{{> (lookup . "bodyPartial") body}}{{/if}}
	</div>
</div>
